A command runs in the container with `sh -c`, reading `quiesce_input` on its
stdin. It ends before the run, as a flush, or, with `quiesce_ready`, it is a
session held open during the run, given `resume_input` at the resume, as a
database client holding a lock. `quiesce_timeout` bounds each step.

Choose it for an application that knows how to make its data consistent,
as a database.
